From 6256394021a13abd52eb34909b640bc6cb5fb537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mstsc-wine <mstsc-wine@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:54:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/43] secur32: Add a CredSSP client security package.

Implements the client side of [MS-CSSP] versions 2-6 on top of Schannel and
Negotiate: TLS handshake, SPNEGO exchange, public key binding (SHA-256 with
client nonce from version 5, CVE-2018-0886) and password delegation.  The
server certificate is verified against the target host name and reported via
SECPKG_ATTR_SERVER_AUTH_FLAGS and SECPKG_ATTR_CERT_TRUST_STATUS, which the
Remote Desktop client uses to warn about unauthenticated servers.

Co-Authored-By: Andrew J. Moore <andrew@forevermoore.net>
---
 dlls/secur32/Makefile.in    |    3 +-
 dlls/secur32/credssp.c      | 1310 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/secur32/secur32.c      |    1 +
 dlls/secur32/secur32_priv.h |    1 +
 4 files changed, 1314 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 dlls/secur32/credssp.c

